# Next.js

- Follow the approved feature specification for scope and visual acceptance
  criteria, `docs/conventions.md` for placement, `docs/design.md` for shared
  visual decisions, and `docs/api.md` for API contracts.
- Use the App Router and Server Components by default.
- Add `'use client'` only for state, effects, event handlers, browser APIs, or
  client-only libraries.
- Keep browser-to-backend communication in the dedicated API client location.
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling. Add shadcn/ui, Radix, Lucide, or another UI
  library only after the product and design require it.
- Do not invent product routes, copy, branding, or external integrations for
  `TBD` business requirements. Decide visual treatment as a senior engineer:
  follow `docs/design.md`, extend the consolidating pattern, and do not ask
  for layout or token details that fit that system.
- Prefer semantic HTML, accessible interactions, optimized images, and
  responsive behavior when the product requires them.
- Treat frontend validation as user experience only; the backend remains the
  authority for validation and authorization.
- Use Vitest and React Testing Library for frontend tests.
- Do not add source-code comments or JSDoc. Use clear names and types instead.
